course: dictionary
lesson: 5905
title: Margin: one word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The word margin has several, and the sentence around it tells you which one is meant. Look for clues: where is it, what is being talked about, and what would fit?
explain: «Priya's mum noticed something odd: Priya was drawing monsters in every margin of her homework.» The clues are homework and drawing. Here a margin is the empty space at the edge of a page, where you do not write.
explain: «The team won by a narrow margin.» Here margin means how far one thing is ahead of another. Swap in "amount of difference" and it still makes sense: won by a narrow amount of difference.
explain: «A poll's margin of error is its wobble.» Here margin of error means an extra amount allowed for mistakes. Always ask which meaning fits the topic: a page, a race, a mistake, or money?
fact: Margin is a noun, and its plural is margins.
fact: «Margin» means the empty space at the edge of a page, often with a line, where you do not write.
fact: «Margin» can also mean the amount one thing is more than another, as in «won by a wide margin».
fact: «Margin of error» means an extra amount allowed for safety or mistakes.
fact: In business, «margin» means profit: what something sells for minus what it cost. A bracelet sold for £1 that cost 20p has a margin of 80p.
exercise: «Priya was drawing monsters in every margin of her homework.» Where were the monsters drawn? | *On the empty edge of the page | In the playground | On the teacher's desk | In the middle of the sums
exercise: «The bracelet sold for £1 and cost 20p, so the margin is 80p.» What does margin mean here? | *Profit, what is left after costs | A mistake | A short wait | The edge of the bracelet
exercise: «The race was won by a wide margin.» What does wide margin suggest? | *The winner was far ahead | The winner was very slow | The race was a tie | The race was cancelled
test: «The teacher wrote a comment in the margin.» Where did the teacher write? | In the school hall | On the board at the front | *At the edge of the page | Under the table
test: «The poll had a margin of error of 3 points.» What does margin of error mean? | The number of people who voted | The name of a political party | A kind of pen | *An allowed amount for mistakes
exam: Ravi says margin only means the edge of a page. Is he right? | Yes, and it also means a bridge | *No, margin also means how far one thing is ahead, an extra amount for mistakes, and profit | No, margin means a loud noise | Yes, it only means the edge of a page
